# Generated from: specs/64-remove-meshy-from-the-pipeline-mcp-config-and-steering/requirements.md
Feature: Remove Meshy from the pipeline and MCP config

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Blender is the only pipeline source
    Given a valid prompt and MCP clients with only Blender and Unreal fakes
    When pipeline.run is called with source "blender"
    Then all six stages run in order and a PipelineResult is returned

  @SCN002
  Scenario Outline: Non-Blender sources are rejected
    Given a valid prompt and MCP client fakes
    When pipeline.run is called with source "<source>"
    Then it raises PipelineError "pipeline.unsupported_source" whose remediation names "blender"
    And no MCP fake was called and no cache entry was written

    Examples:
      | source |
      | meshy  |
      | other  |

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Meshy client types are gone
    Given the nmg_game_dev.pipeline package
    When it is imported
    Then McpClients has no meshy field, MeshyMcp and generate_meshy do not exist, Server is "blender" | "unreal", and Source is "blender"

  @SCN004
  Scenario: The MCP configuration has no Meshy server
    Given the repo .mcp.json
    When the scaffold guard tests run
    Then only the blender and unreal servers are declared and no MESHY_API_KEY or meshy-mcp-server text appears

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Steering does not offer Meshy as a source
    Given the steering snippets
    When the guard test scans them
    Then none contains "--source meshy", 'source="meshy"', "meshy-mcp-server", or "MESHY_API_KEY"
